eports that constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand has pushed contract DDR5 pricing sharply higher, with device makers including Samsung and Apple expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products, and that memory supply tightness now warrants the same scheduling and planning attention as GPU allocation, with procurement structure able to move rack pricing by $1+ million.\"\n  ],\n  \"link_rule\": \"No link is required: an empty link counts as linked as required (a statement no open thesis covers is kept without links by design).\",\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-rack-price\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates that a single Nvidia Vera Rubin VR200 NVL72 rack will cost hyperscale cloud providers around $7.8 million, up from roughly $4 million for the current GB300 NVL72 generation — the next-generation rack price nearly doubling.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-chip-prices\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley Research estimates Nvidia will charge about $55,000 per Rubin GPU and $5,000 per Vera CPU when the products are sold in volume.\",\n    \"links\": []\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-memory-content\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage that was virtually absent from earlier systems.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"new-mem-prices\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-ship-schedule\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley's analysis indicates Vera Rubin first shipments are scheduled for the third quarter of 2026, with volume ramping in the fourth quarter.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"clean-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-bom-share\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley's bill-of-materials breakdown shows memory's share of the rack rose from 5–10% on the GB200 to 25–30% on the VR200, while the GPU's share fell from roughly 63% to 51%.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"new-mem-prices\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-memory-supply\",\n    \"summary\": \"MarketScale, drawing on the Morgan Stanley breakdown, reports that constrained supply of DRAM, NAND and high-bandwidth memory against AI-driven demand is now raising component costs across the market; contract DDR5 pricing has climbed sharply and device makers including Samsung and Apple are expected to pass higher memory costs into upcoming products. It presents memory availability as a scheduling and planning risk on par with GPU allocation.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"new-mem-prices\",\n     \"clean-3\"\n    ]\n   },\n   {\n    \"id\": \"ev-self-source-price\",\n    \"summary\": \"Morgan Stanley notes that a hyperscaler self-sourcing certain memory modules could bring the Vera Rubin rack price down to around $6.7 million, showing that procurement structure materially moves the rack price.\",\n    \"links\": [\n     \"new-mem-prices\"\n    ]\n   }\n  ]\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 10,\n  \"claims\": [\n   {\n    \"claim_id\": \"M1\",\n    \"claim\": \"Morgan Stanley puts memory content per Vera Rubin rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation.\"\n   }\n  ],\n  \"stored_reference_items\": [\n   \"Morgan Stanley estimates memory content per Vera Rubin VR200 rack at about $2 million, a 435% jump from the prior generation, driven by a threefold increase in LPDDR5X capacity to 54 terabytes per rack plus roughly $1 million or more in 3D NAND storage; memory rose to 25-30% of the bill of materials from 5-10% on the GB200, while the GPU's share fell to about 51% from roughly 63%.\"\n  ],\n  \"link_rule\": \"No link is required: an empty link counts as linked as required (a statement no open thesis covers is kept without links by design).\",\n  \"answer_usable\": true,\n  \"kept_evidence\": [\n   {\n  